# Keys allowed to ratify (section 8).
#
# This repository signs with GPG, so `git verify-commit` resolves the signature
# through the keyring and never reads this file: git consults an allowed-signers
# file only under `gpg.format = ssh`. The entry below is therefore a declaration
# and not a mechanism. It records which identity may ratify, in a versioned file
# where adding one is a diff in review, and enforcement stays advisory in the
# sense section 8 already accepts and displays. Switching `gpg.format` to ssh
# and pointing `gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile` here is what would make it
# load-bearing, and that trade was weighed and declined: it would change the
# signature of every commit in the repository, not only the ratifications.
#
# Layout follows git's allowed-signers file: principal, then the key.
